{{ArgTitle|4|SaveGame|{{GVI|arma3|2.18}}}}
Triggered just BEFORE the game saving process started but [[isSaving]] is already set to [[true]]. To know when the saving is finished check when [[isSaving]] returns [[false]]. 

<sqf>
addMissionEventHandler ["SaveGame", {
	params ["_saveType"];
}];
</sqf>

* saveType: [[String]] - one of "autosaveold", "autosave", "save", "save2", "save3", "save4", "save5", "save6", "continue" or "".


{{ArgTitle|4|ScriptError|{{GVI|arma3|2.14}}}}
Triggered when a script error occurs. See also the {{hl|{{Link|Arma 3: Startup Parameters#Developer Options|-showScriptErrors}}}} {{Link|Arma 3: Startup Parameters|startup parameter}}.

{{Feature|informative|
Event Handlers have a recursion check. Most of them have a level limit set to '''1''';
'''ScriptError''' has it set to '''2''' - meaning that an error occuring inside the Event Handler will trigger once more the EH, but no more than two times total.
}}

<sqf>
addMissionEventHandler ["ScriptError", {
	params ["_errorText", "_sourceFile", "_lineNumber", "_errorPos", "_content", "_stackTraceOutput"];
}];
</sqf>

* errorText: [[String]] - e.g. "Zero Divisor"
* sourceFile: [[String]] - empty string if spawned [[Code]]
* lineNumber: [[Number]] - script's line number
* errorPos: [[Number]] - script's error byte position in the script ''content''
* content: [[String]] - the whole script's [[Code]] as [[String]]
* stackTraceOutput: [[Array]] - see [[diag_stacktrace]] output

{{ArgTitle|4|ScriptSpawned|{{GVI|arma3|2.22}}}}
Executes when any script is spawned.
<sqf>
addMissionEventHandler ["ScriptSpawned", {
	params ["_data"];
}];
</sqf>

* _data: [[Array]] with [fileName, content, hash, parentFileName, parentLine, parentScript]
** fileName: [[String]] - file name of the spawned script, empty when not available
** content: [[String]] - content of the spawned script
** hash: [[String]] - hash value of the [[Script Handle]]
** parentFileName [[String]] - file name of the parent script, empty when not available
** parentLine: [[Number]] - line number of the parent script
** parentScript: [[String]] - content of the parent script

